    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To create a page link, you need to know:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "how to structure and use the AsciiDoc xref macro,"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "how to assign the resource ID of a page to an AsciiDoc xref macro,"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the resource ID of the page you’re linking to (the target page), and"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "the resource ID of the page where you want the link to be displayed (the current page)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An AsciiDoc xref macro is used to create a source-to-source cross reference from a resource to a publishable resource. The term "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "cross reference"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which is often abbreviated to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "xref"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", means to use the AsciiDoc xref macro to reference the source file of a publishable resource. The xref macro accepts an "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Antora resource ID"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "resource-id.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " specifying a publishable page, attachment, or, occasionally, an image, as a value. When Antora runs, an xref macro and its value are converted into a link to the target resource’s published URL."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Figure 1"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "#fig-xref-macro"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " shows the structure of an xref macro."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "alt": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Diagram of an AsciiDoc xref macro with an Antora resource ID for a page"
                  }
                ],
                "attributes": {},
                "context": "image",
                "id": "fig-xref-macro",
                "roles": [],
                "src": "xref-macro-with-resource-id-for-page.svg",
                "svg": null,
                "target": "xref-macro-with-resource-id-for-page.svg",
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Xref macro structure for referencing a page"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "At a minimum, an xref macro consists of the macro’s prefix ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "xref:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "), the resource ID of the target page, and a set of square brackets ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "[]"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "). "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "target",
                    "kind": "anchor"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "target page"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": [
                      "term"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " is the page source file that’s being referenced by the current page. The target page is referenced by assigning its resource ID to an xref macro in the content of the current page. "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "current",
                    "kind": "anchor"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "current page"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": [
                      "term"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " is the page source file containing the xref macro that references the target page."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "admonition",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You should not use the shorthand xref syntax to create a link to a resource outside of the current document, such as another page (e.g., "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "<<other-page.adoc#>>"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "). Although technically the shorthand xref will work in this scenario, its use clouds the distinction between internal and external references. Furthermore, not all extensions support the shorthand xref when used this way. "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Always prefer the xref macro to make references to resources outside of the current page."
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null,
                "type": "important"
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Each part of the xref macro shown in "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Figure 1"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "#fig-xref-macro"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " is described in more detail below."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "An xref macro begins with the macro’s name, "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "xref"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ", followed by a single colon ("
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": ":"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ")."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "xref:"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "The xref macro accepts the resource ID of a page as its value. The value is entered directly after the colon that follows the macro’s name ("
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "xref:"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "). How many of the target page’s "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "resource ID coordinates"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "resource-id-coordinates.html"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " you need to specify depends on the component version and module of the target page in relation to the current page. The "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "page$"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " family coordinate isn’t required in the resource ID when the target resource is a page. Also, remember that the "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "file coordinate"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "resource-id-coordinates.html#id-resource"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " of a target page is calculated from the "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "pages"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "emphasis",
                          "roles": [
                            "path"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " family directory."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "resource ID of target page"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "A "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "fragment"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "strong",
                          "roles": [
                            "term"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " is an element ID that links to a section, block, or inline location within the target page. Fragments are also referred to as "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "deep links"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "strong",
                          "roles": [
                            "term"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ". A fragment is optional. The fragment starts with the hash symbol ("
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "#"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ") and is entered directly after the resource ID of the target page. A target page’s reference text, whether assigned by default or using the "
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "reftext"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " attribute, isn’t used as "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "link text"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "#link-text"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " when a fragment is specified."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "id": "id-fragment",
                          "kind": "anchor"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "#fragment"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "The xref macro is completed with a set of square brackets ("
                        },
                        {
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "[]"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "monospace",
                          "roles": []
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ") at the end of the target page’s resource ID, or, if specified, at the end of the "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "fragment"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "#id-fragment"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": ". You can enter optional text between these brackets or leave them empty. When Antora converts the xref macro and its value into a link, the text entered between the square brackets is displayed in the current page when it’s published to your site. If no link text is specified between the macro’s square brackets, and the value of the xref macro doesn’t contain a fragment, then the target page’s "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "default reference text"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "link-content.html#default"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " or text assigned to the "
                        },
                        {
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "reftext attribute"
                            }
                          ],
                          "kind": "xref",
                          "target": "reftext-and-navtitle.html"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": " is displayed in the current page when it’s published. If a fragment is appended to the resource ID of the target page and no link text is entered between the brackets, then the URL of the published target page is displayed."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "id": "link-text",
                          "kind": "anchor"
                        },
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "[link text]"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The next section explains how to create a cross reference step-by-step."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
